/*
✅✅Primitive Types

Primitive types represent single, simple values.

| Type        | Example         |
| ----------- | --------------- |
| `string`    | `"Raju"`        |
| `number`    | `25`, `3.14`    |
| `boolean`   | `true`, `false` |
| `null`      | `null`          |
| `undefined` | `undefined`     |
| `bigint`    | `100n`          |
| `symbol`    | `Symbol("id")`  |


📌Key point: Primitive values are immutable and are not objects.


Examples :

➡️string
let name: string = "Raju";

➡️number
let age: number = 25;
let price: number = 99.99;

➡️boolean
let isLoggedIn: boolean = true;

➡️null
let data: null = null;

➡️undefined
let result: undefined = undefined;

➡️bigint
let largeNumber: bigint = 12345678901234567890n;

➡️symbol
let id: symbol = Symbol("userId");

*/ 
